📊 Project Description: Spreadsheet Data Analysis – Manhattan Vacation Rental Market

Conducted a comprehensive data analysis of the Manhattan vacation rental market using spreadsheet tools to identify the most profitable investment opportunities. Cleaned and prepared raw Airbnb listing and calendar datasets by standardizing neighborhood names, handling missing bedroom values, and documenting all data transformation steps to ensure data integrity and reproducibility.

Utilized pivot tables and data visualization techniques to evaluate rental demand across neighborhoods and property sizes, using customer reviews as a proxy for rental frequency. Identified top-performing neighborhoods such as Harlem, Hell’s Kitchen, and Lower East Side, and determined that 1-bedroom units were the most popular property size across most locations.

Performed revenue analysis by calculating nightly earnings and estimating annual revenue using conditional formulas and aggregation functions. Generated actionable recommendations for stakeholders on optimal property investment strategies based on demand trends and revenue potential. Delivered findings through an executive summary, structured reporting, and visual dashboards to support data-driven decision-making.

